I load `profile` and `profileIndex` once into locals and use `__builtin_expect` to keep the common valid-type and valid-profile branches on the fast path, avoiding redundant member loads.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return type;

    const Profile *p = profile;
    const FIT_UINT8 idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL || idx >= p->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[idx].type;
}
```